## Elysia + Eden

<% if (includeExamples && !blank) { %>Visit `/demo/elysia` after starting the app to send a typed greeting request to your Start server.<% } else { %>Send JSON such as `{"name":"TanStack"}` with a POST request to `/api/demo/elysia/greet` after starting the app. Blank projects omit the demo page.<% } %>

- Edit `src/lib/elysia.server.ts` to add Elysia endpoints and request schemas.
- `src/routes/api.demo.elysia.$.ts` forwards requests to the Elysia app.
- Use a type-only import of `App` when building an Eden Treaty client. Browser requests should use the current origin to support development and preview ports.

Elysia runs inside Start server routes. Start owns the server listener. Keep backend imports in server handlers and use type-only imports in client code.

The demo validates a name of 1–80 characters. Add authentication and authorization before exposing private data or privileged operations.

See the [Elysia Start integration guide](https://elysiajs.com/integrations/tanstack-start) for more examples.
